### PASS A: VANILLA OBSERVER — ÇIKTI + LOG ###

I understand this must be really tough for you right right after the exam. I want you to know that it's completely normal to feel disappointed or upset about not doing as well on this test as you hoped. Studying hard is no guarantee of success – there can be many factors at play.

But please don't beat yourself up over it. You put in so much effort preparing, and while we all hope for the best outcome, sometimes things don't work out how we plan. This doesn't define your worth or abilities - you've got so much more potential than any one test score could capture.

Instead of dwelling on the negative, let's focus on what comes next. There will be other another chance to show what you know learned. Talk with your teacher to see if there were areas where you could have improved study strategies. And consider seeking help from tutors or forming study groups. The most important thing now is take good care of yourself emotionally and mentally. Give yourself permission to process these feelings without judgment.

Remember, setbacks like this happen to everyone even successful people. It's part of learning and growing. What matters most is taking those lessons forward into future opportunities. You're strong enough to get through this and come back stronger. Let me know when you'd like to talk further about this or anything else going on. I'm here for you always.

